    "notes": "The National Museum of Malaysia main building as recorded in January 2008. Includes the long symmetrical palace-inspired roof wings, steep projecting entrance gable with crossed apex and three vertical entrance bays, twin mosaic fields, stairs and side/rear exterior. The museum collections, detached Istana Satu and later MRT station are outside scope. Mosaic fields are represented by generic material without copying the artworks. Use the original footprint and the public-domain January 2008 overview. The independent 2022 photograph corroborates the surviving gable and wing arrangement."
  },
